From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Valentin Rothberg <vrothberg@redhat.com>
Date: Thu, 9 Jan 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Skip TestTerminalSignal in podman containers

The test fails when running in a podman container with --init, as used
by mock for RPM builds. The --init flag spawns a PID 1 init process
that interferes with terminal signal handling, causing wait4() operations
to hang indefinitely.

Detect podman by reading /proc/1/comm and skip the test in this environment.

Related: https://issues.redhat.com/browse/ROK-1280
---
 src/os/signal/signal_cgo_test.go | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/os/signal/signal_cgo_test.go b/src/os/signal/signal_cgo_test.go
index 0000000000..1111111111 100644
--- a/src/os/signal/signal_cgo_test.go
+++ b/src/os/signal/signal_cgo_test.go
@@ -17,6 +17,8 @@ import (
 	"internal/syscall/unix"
 	"internal/testenv"
 	"internal/testpty"
+	"io/ioutil"
+	"strings"
 	"os"
 	"os/signal"
 	"runtime"
@@ -79,6 +81,13 @@ func TestTerminalSignal(t *testing.T) {
 		t.Skip("skipping: wait hangs on dragonfly; see https://go.dev/issue/56132")
 	}

+	// Check if we're in a container environment where wait4() might hang
+	if data, err := ioutil.ReadFile("/proc/1/comm"); err == nil {
+		if strings.Contains(string(data), "podman") {
+			t.Skip("Skipping TestTerminalSignal in container environment - wait4() operations may hang")
+		}
+	}
+
 	scale := 1
 	if s := os.Getenv("GO_TEST_TIMEOUT_SCALE"); s != "" {
 		if sc, err := strconv.Atoi(s); err == nil {
--
2.50.1
